## Project Overview
Sajuline renewal monorepo for a hybrid fortune-telling platform where AI and experts collaborate. Frontend is a Nuxt 4 SSR web app; backend is a FastAPI async API. Local development is orchestrated with Docker Compose.

### Primary References
- Project overview and high-level docs: [README.md](mdc:README.md)
- Backend entrypoint and app init: [backend/src/main.py](mdc:backend/src/main.py)
- Backend settings and env keys: [backend/src/config/settings.py](mdc:backend/src/config/settings.py)
- Infra (dev compose stack): [infra/docker-compose.yml](mdc:infra/docker-compose.yml)
- Frontend configuration: [frontend/nuxt.config.ts](mdc:frontend/nuxt.config.ts)
- Frontend scripts/deps: [frontend/package.json](mdc:frontend/package.json)
- Backend packaging/deps: [backend/pyproject.toml](mdc:backend/pyproject.toml)
- Backend Dockerfile(s): [backend/Dockerfile](mdc:backend/Dockerfile)

### Architecture at a Glance
- Frontend: Nuxt 4 + Vue 3 + TypeScript (SSR by default; mixes SWR/CSR on select routes)
- Backend: FastAPI + Uvicorn, layered (API/services/repositories/schemas)
- Data: MariaDB (primary), MSSQL (ARS integration)
- Cache: Redis
- Observability/Safety: Sentry, structured logging (Loguru+JSON), rate-limiting (SlowAPI), CORS, Trusted Host

### Run/Develop
- Dev stack (recommended):
  - cd infra → `docker compose up --build -d`
  - Health: backend `http://localhost:8000/health`, frontend `http://localhost:3000/`
- Local, without Compose:
  - Frontend: `cd frontend && npm install && npm run dev`
  - Backend: `cd backend && pip install uv && uv pip install -r pyproject.toml --extra dev && uvicorn src.main:app --reload`

### API Surface
- Base path: `/api/v1/*`
- Health: `GET /health`, readiness: `GET /readiness`
- Functional domains: `auth`, `users`, `counselors`, `notices`

### Conventions for This Workspace
- Prefer readability and correctness; avoid placeholders/TODOs in committed code.
- Keep environment variable names consistent with [backend/src/config/settings.py](mdc:backend/src/config/settings.py).
- Follow tooling: black/isort/flake8/mypy/pytest; keep logs under `backend/logs/`.
- Treat KCP binaries and secrets as sensitive; never hardcode credentials.
- When in doubt about project intent, consult [README.md](mdc:README.md) first.
- Default communication language with the user is Korean unless explicitly requested otherwise.
